## Phase 0 — setup
- Worktree .worktrees/lane-dogfood2 on branch lane/dogfood2 from main (d3fb7b0).
- Symptoms from user real-world test (HOME=/root, real data dir):
  (1) restored tabs render at top but CLICKING them does nothing (v2: switches session).
  (2) cursor blinks at wrong position at boot (v2: composer row).
- Sandbox plan: /tmp/opencode/dogfood2/home with COPY of real DB+state (never write real dir).

## Phase 1 — root-cause analysis (code read, v2 ref citations)
- BUG 1 (dead tab clicks): app.rs:300-303 gates `strip_live` on
  `matches!(route, Route::Session)` — but the strip PAINTS on Home too
  (home.rs:349-374, F9) whenever tabs_enabled && tabs non-empty. v2 mounts
  SessionTabs app-wide: app.tsx:1353-1355 `<Show when={tabsVisible() && !tabsVertical()}>`
  above the route `<Switch>`; `tabsAvailable()` app.tsx:576-579 = `enabled() &&
  tabs().length > 0 && route.data.type !== "plugin"` — never session-gated. select()
  = bare route.navigate (context/session-tabs.tsx:393-396). => clicks on Home no-op.
- BUG 2 (cursor row): home.rs:344-347 `set_caret_cell(caret_screen)` runs BEFORE the
  strip shift (home.rs:354-373): the frame rows shift down 1 but the caret stays at the
  pre-shift row = exactly the strip height above the composer row. ALSO the shift
  path renders the home view at FULL height then truncates (home.rs:365-367), clipping
  the composer's bottom row; v2 lays Home out in height-1 (the strip is row 0 of the
  same column, app.tsx:1349-1361) so nothing clips. Session route caret is bottom-docked
  (session.rs:620-632 `height - prompt_height + cell_y`) — strip-independent, correct.
- Suspect 2 (hydration of not-yet-loaded sessions): already covered — F12 transcript
  fetch loop app.rs:2687-2702 fetches every open-session id once; navigate() (store.rs:2940-2979)
  is a bare route set + tab open like v2. No preloaded-registry requirement.
- Suspect 1 (strip_hit geometry): strip_hit mirrors adaptive_session_tab_layout, the same
  solver paint_live_tabs_bar uses (session.rs:88-96 paints via session_tabs_solid with the
  same layout); row 0 on both routes. Geometry consistent — not the cause.

