## Phase 3 — REPRODUCED both bugs (sandbox: real-DB copy, empty cwd, restored tabs)
Sandbox learnings (shape fidelity):
- Our roots are `opencode-rust`-suffixed (data AND state): tabs restore reads
  `$XDG_STATE_HOME/opencode-rust/stable/tui/tabs.json` (channel default "stable");
  v2 reads `.../opencode/latest|local/tui/tabs.json`. Both seeded per side.
- First our-binary boot in a v2-shaped home runs the one-way v2→rust DB migration
  (1.5G copy) — user's env has the marker; sandbox pre-seeded marker + DB.
- Ref must run WITHOUT bun defines (the TUI-spawned background server re-execs without
  them → channel skew local vs stable → discovery loop); ref DB = opencode-local.db.
- v2 tsconfig.json seeded in the empty cwd (the rig's jsxImportSource fix).

Evidence (80x24, cwd=/tmp/opencode/dogfood2/home/work, 2 restored tabs referencing
sessions whose directory is /opt/lobechat + /opt/new-api — none for the cwd):
- OURS boot: strip row0 painted (two tab titles + " + "). Composer input row = 14
  ("Ask anything…" row), hardware cursor = (6,13) → ONE ROW ABOVE the input row
  (= exactly the strip height; set_caret_cell ran before the strip shift).
- OURS click SGR col5 row1 (tab 1 body): NOTHING changes (same rows, same cursor).
- REF boot: strip row0 painted; input row = 13 (home lays out in height-1); cursor
  (6,13) ON the input row. REF same click: route switches to the session (renders
  its session card — "Session not found: …" for a cross-project session id, i.e.
  v2 routes even when the cwd's project scope can't see it).
- Extra divergence captured: ours lays home out at FULL height then truncates →
  bottom status row clipped (ours shows version row at 22; ref status bar at 23).

## Phase 4 — fix plan (1:1 v2 semantics)
- app.rs mouse_event: strip_live must include Route::Home (v2 app.tsx:576-579
  tabsAvailable gates on `route.data.type !== "plugin"` only + 1353-1355 app-wide mount).
- home.rs render_home: lay the home view out in height-1 when the strip shows (v2:
  strip is row 0 of the SAME column — app.tsx:1349-1361), prepend the strip row, and
  shift the caret cell +1 (caret inside the shifted subtree).
